IMPORT prelude

-- Singapore Corporation of Rehabilitative Enterprises Act 1975 (Singapore) -- what the Act decides for a prisoner, an inmate, a
-- discharged offender, an employee of the Corporation, a business that copies its symbol, and a counterparty dealing with it:
-- who is a "prisoner" or an "inmate" (s 2), which functions and powers reach whom (ss 15, 16(c), (g), (h), (k)), using the
-- Corporation's symbol and the penalty (s 17A), what may be delegated and to whom (s 17), the quorum (s 6(2)), execution under the
-- common seal (s 35(2)), remuneration not tied to profits (s 21), personal immunity (s 22), the financial year (s 24) and the
-- Government's share of a transferred employee's pension (s 14(2)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation ("version in force from 17/6/2024"), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/SCREA1975.txt. The revised edition "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021";
-- the latest amendment annotated is Act 16 of 2024 (Law Enforcement and Other Matters Act 2024), annotated "wef 17/06/2024" on
-- ss 17A and 36 and listed in the legislative history with commencement 17 June 2024. Section numbers follow the BODY: in the
-- arrangement of sections at the top of the deposit, Part 4 is column-shifted (the titles "Functions of Corporation" and "Powers"
-- carry no number, "15." sits against "Appointment of committees", "16." against "Corporation's symbol", and "17." and "17A." have
-- no title). The body has s 15 Functions, s 16 Powers, s 17 committees and delegation, s 17A the symbol.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0208 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked
-- a sharper question yet. SCOPED to the provisions a prisoner, inmate, discharged offender, employee, or outside business meets.
-- Not encoded: establishment and business names (s 3), appointment, tenure, revocation and pay of members (ss 4, 5) beyond the size
-- of the Corporation, meetings beyond the quorum (s 6(1), (3)-(7)), validity of members' acts (s 8), Ministerial directions (s 9),
-- the 1976 transfer of training institutions, employees, contracts and proceedings (ss 10-13) and s 14(1), the general powers in
-- s 16 other than (c), (g), (h) and (k), the chief executive officer and staff (ss 18, 19), pension schemes (s 20), expenses,
-- estimates, grants, loans, shares and investment (ss 25-29), s 35(1), (3), (4) and regulations (s 36). No regulations made under
-- s 36, and no order prescribing an institution for the definition of "inmate", were retrieved.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Singapore Corporation of Rehabilitative Enterprises Act 1975`

§§ `2 -- prisoner and inmate`

-- s 2: "inmate" means "a person who is detained in any approved institution under the Misuse of Drugs Act 1973 or in such other
-- institution or place as may be prescribed"; "prisoner" means "any person, whether convicted or not, under detention in any prison
-- or reformative training centre".
-- A person held in a police lock-up is neither unless the place is prescribed; that no lock-up is prescribed is an ASSUMPTION
-- (nothing prescribed was retrieved).
DECLARE Detention IS ONE OF
    `serving a sentence in prison`
    `remanded in prison awaiting trial`
    `detained in a reformative training centre`
    `detained in an approved institution under the Misuse of Drugs Act 1973`
    `detained in a prescribed institution or place`
    `held in a police lock-up that is not prescribed`
    `released from custody`

DECLARE Status IS ONE OF
    `a prisoner`
    `an inmate`
    `neither a prisoner nor an inmate`

GIVEN `the detention` IS A Detention
GIVETH A Status
`the person's status under section 2` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the detention`
    WHEN `serving a sentence in prison` THEN `a prisoner`
    WHEN `remanded in prison awaiting trial` THEN `a prisoner`
    WHEN `detained in a reformative training centre` THEN `a prisoner`
    WHEN `detained in an approved institution under the Misuse of Drugs Act 1973` THEN `an inmate`
    WHEN `detained in a prescribed institution or place` THEN `an inmate`
    OTHERWISE `neither a prisoner nor an inmate`

§§ `15 and 16(c), (g), (h), (k) -- what the Corporation may do for whom`

-- s 15: the functions include "(c) to provide technical training in skilled trades for suitable prisoners and inmates"; "(e) to
-- provide any prisoner with work for the purposes of section 67 of the Prisons Act 1933"; "(g) to provide or secure the provision of
-- rehabilitative and aftercare services to prisoners and inmates before and after their discharge from custody".
-- s 16: the Corporation may "(c) pay such salaries, wages, remuneration or allowances as the Corporation thinks fit to prisoners and
-- inmates who work for the Corporation"; "(g) make loans to persons, other than prisoners and inmates, who are employed by the
-- Corporation (including loans to assist them to acquire housing accommodation)"; "(h) promote recreational activities for and
-- activities conducive to the welfare of persons, other than prisoners and inmates, who are or have been engaged in the employment
-- of the Corporation"; "(k) make grants or lend money to, or enter into guarantees on behalf of, prisoners and inmates after their
-- discharge from custody for the purposes of any vocation, trade or business carrying on by them".
-- Each is a power or function, not an entitlement: the encoding answers "may the Corporation", never "must it".
-- Reading "after their discharge" in s 16(k) and "before and after their discharge" in s 15(g) as reaching a person who was a
-- prisoner or inmate and has been discharged is the encoding's reading.
DECLARE Person HAS
    `is a prisoner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an inmate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was a prisoner or inmate and has been discharged from custody` IS A BOOLEAN
    `works for the Corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is employed by the Corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has been employed by the Corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is suitable for training in a skilled trade` IS A BOOLEAN
    `carries on a vocation, trade or business` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is a prisoner or inmate` IF
    `the person`'s `is a prisoner` OR `the person`'s `is an inmate`

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Corporation may provide technical training in a skilled trade under section 15(c)` IF
    `the person is a prisoner or inmate` `the person` AND `the person`'s `is suitable for training in a skilled trade`

-- s 15(e) names "any prisoner" only; an inmate is not a prisoner under s 2.
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Corporation may provide work for the purposes of section 67 of the Prisons Act 1933` IF
    `the person`'s `is a prisoner`

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Corporation may provide aftercare services under section 15(g)` IF
    `the person is a prisoner or inmate` `the person`
    OR `the person`'s `was a prisoner or inmate and has been discharged from custody`

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Corporation may pay the person for work under section 16(c)` IF
    `the person is a prisoner or inmate` `the person` AND `the person`'s `works for the Corporation`

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Corporation may make the person a staff or housing loan under section 16(g)` IF
    `the person`'s `is employed by the Corporation` AND (NOT (`the person is a prisoner or inmate` `the person`))

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Corporation may promote welfare activities for the person under section 16(h)` IF
        (`the person`'s `is employed by the Corporation` OR `the person`'s `has been employed by the Corporation`)
    AND (NOT (`the person is a prisoner or inmate` `the person`))

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Corporation may make a business grant, loan or guarantee under section 16(k)` IF
        `the person`'s `was a prisoner or inmate and has been discharged from custody`
    AND `the person`'s `carries on a vocation, trade or business`

§§ `17A -- the Corporation's symbol or representation`

-- s 17A(1): "The Corporation has the exclusive right to the use of one or more symbols or representations as the Corporation may
-- select or devise".
-- s 17A(2): "A person who, without the prior written permission of the Corporation -- (a) uses a symbol or representation identical to
-- the Corporation's symbol or representation; or (b) uses a symbol or representation which so resembles the Corporation's symbol or
-- representation as to deceive or to cause confusion, or to be likely to deceive or to cause confusion, shall be guilty of an offence
-- and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or to both
-- and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not exceeding $250 for every day or part of a day during which the
-- offence continues after conviction." [Act 16 of 2024 wef 17/06/2024]
-- Permission must be prior and written: oral or after-the-event permission does not count. The section states no mental element.
DECLARE SymbolUse HAS
    `identical to the Corporation's symbol` IS A BOOLEAN
    `so resembles it as to deceive or cause confusion, or be likely to` IS A BOOLEAN
    `prior written permission of the Corporation` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the use` IS A SymbolUse
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the use is an offence under section 17A(2)` IF
        (`the use`'s `identical to the Corporation's symbol` OR `the use`'s `so resembles it as to deceive or cause confusion, or be likely to`)
    AND (NOT `the use`'s `prior written permission of the Corporation`)

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine under section 17A(2)` MEANS 10000

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months under section 17A(2)` MEANS 6

-- "every day or part of a day": the input counts each day, or part of a day, after conviction as one.
GIVEN `days or parts of days continued after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum further fine under section 17A(2)` MEANS 250 * `days or parts of days continued after conviction`

§§ `17 -- delegation`

-- s 17(2): the Corporation may delegate "to any such committee, the Chairperson, any member or the chief executive officer all or any
-- of the powers, functions and duties by this Act vested in the Corporation, except the power to borrow money".
-- s 17(4): it may delegate "to any employee of the Corporation all or any of the Corporation's powers ... except the power to borrow
-- money or to raise or grant loans or advances to or subscribe to or underwrite the issue of stocks, shares, bonds or debentures of
-- industrial enterprises".
-- Reading the s 17(4) exception as excluding granting loans or advances generally (and not only to industrial enterprises) is the
-- encoding's reading of a long phrase; the alternative reading is noted in NOTES.md.
DECLARE Delegate IS ONE OF
    `a committee`
    `the Chairperson`
    `a member`
    `the chief executive officer`
    `an employee`

DECLARE Power IS ONE OF
    `borrowing money`
    `granting loans or advances`
    `underwriting shares of an industrial enterprise`
    `entering into a contract`
    `levying charges for services`

GIVEN `the delegate` IS A Delegate, `the power` IS A Power
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the power may be delegated under section 17` IF
    CONSIDER `the power`
    WHEN `borrowing money` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `granting loans or advances` THEN
        CONSIDER `the delegate`
        WHEN `an employee` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE
    WHEN `underwriting shares of an industrial enterprise` THEN
        CONSIDER `the delegate`
        WHEN `an employee` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `4(1) and 6(2) -- size of the Corporation and quorum`

-- s 4(1): the members are "(a) a Chairperson; (b) a Deputy Chairperson who must be an officer from the Ministry of Home Affairs;
-- (c) the Commissioner of Prisons or his or her representative; and (d) at least 2 and not more than 12 other members".
-- s 6(2): "The quorum at every meeting of the Corporation is one-third of the total number of members or 3 members, whichever is the
-- higher."
-- One-third is compared without rounding: present times 3 must reach the total. Temporary members (s 4(3)) are not modelled.
GIVEN `other members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the number of other members is within section 4(1)(d)` IF
    `other members` AT LEAST 2 AND `other members` AT MOST 12

GIVEN `other members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the total number of members` MEANS 3 + `other members`

GIVEN `total members` IS A NUMBER, `members present` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the quorum under section 6(2) is present` IF
    `members present` * 3 AT LEAST `total members` AND `members present` AT LEAST 3

§§ `35(2) -- execution under the common seal`

-- s 35(2): "every instrument to which the common seal is affixed must be signed by a member and must be countersigned by the chief
-- executive officer or by some other person duly authorised by the Corporation for the purpose, and the signing is sufficient evidence
-- that the seal was duly and properly affixed".
-- The chief executive officer is not a member under s 4(1) (an observation from the list in s 4(1), which does not name the office).
DECLARE Signatory IS ONE OF
    `the Chairperson`
    `the Deputy Chairperson`
    `the Commissioner of Prisons as member`
    `another member`
    `the chief executive officer`
    `a person the Corporation authorised to countersign`
    `an unauthorised employee`

GIVEN `the signatory` IS A Signatory
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the signatory is a member` IF
    CONSIDER `the signatory`
    WHEN `the Chairperson` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Deputy Chairperson` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Commissioner of Prisons as member` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `another member` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the signatory` IS A Signatory
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the signatory may countersign` IF
    CONSIDER `the signatory`
    WHEN `the chief executive officer` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a person the Corporation authorised to countersign` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `sealed` IS A BOOLEAN, `signer` IS A Signatory, `countersigner` IS A Signatory
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the instrument is executed as section 35(2) requires` IF
    `sealed` AND `the signatory is a member` `signer` AND `the signatory may countersign` `countersigner`

§§ `21 and 22 -- remuneration and personal immunity`

-- s 21: "Any salary, fee, wage or other remuneration or allowance paid by the Corporation to any member, employee or agent must not
-- be computed by reference to the profits of the Corporation."
-- s 22: no matter or thing done by "any member or by any employee of the Corporation or any other person acting under its direction"
-- shall, "if the matter or thing was done or the contract was entered into in good faith for the purpose of carrying out the
-- provisions of this Act", subject that person "personally to any action, liability, claim or demand".
-- s 22 protects the individual; it does not say the Corporation itself escapes liability.
GIVEN `computed by reference to the Corporation's profits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the remuneration is permitted by section 21` IF NOT `computed by reference to the Corporation's profits`

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    `a member`
    `an employee`
    `a person acting under the Corporation's direction`
    `an independent contractor not under its direction`

GIVEN `the actor` IS AN Actor, `in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN, `for the purpose of carrying out the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the actor is personally immune under section 22` IF
        (CONSIDER `the actor`
         WHEN `an independent contractor not under its direction` THEN FALSE
         OTHERWISE TRUE)
    AND `in good faith`
    AND `for the purpose of carrying out the Act`

§§ `24 -- financial year`

-- s 24: "The financial year of the Corporation begins on 1 April each year and ends on 31 March of the following year."
-- The answer is the calendar year in which the financial year began.
GIVEN `calendar year` IS A NUMBER, `month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the year in which the financial year began` MEANS
    IF `month` AT LEAST 4 THEN `calendar year` ELSE `calendar year` - 1

§§ `14(2) -- the Government's share of a transferred employee's pension`

-- s 14(2): where a person was transferred under s 11(1), "the Government is liable to pay to the Corporation such portion of any
-- gratuity, pension or allowance payable to that person ... as the same bears to the proportion which the aggregate amount of his or
-- her pensionable emoluments during his or her service with the Government bears to the aggregate amount of his or her pensionable
-- emoluments during his or her service under both the Government and the Corporation."
-- The wording is circular ("as the same bears to the proportion"); the encoding reads it as the benefit times Government emoluments
-- over total emoluments. The payment runs from the Government to the Corporation, not to the employee.
GIVEN `the benefit` IS A NUMBER, `Government emoluments` IS A NUMBER, `Corporation emoluments` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Government's share under section 14(2)` MEANS
    `the benefit` * `Government emoluments` / (`Government emoluments` + `Corporation emoluments`)
